---
title: Italian Sandwich with Prosciutto Di Parma
servings: 4
prepTime: 20 min
difficulty: Easy
Rating: 8/10
source: https://www.kitchenstories.com/en/recipes/italian-sandwich-with-prosciutto-di-parma
tags: Pork
---

Cut the @ciabatta bread{} lengthwise and drizzle with @olive oil{2%tbsp}.
Roast oiled side down in a hot pan for approximately ~{3-5%minutes}, or brown in a toaster or under a broiler.

Meanwhile, cut @mozzarella{4%oz}(sliced) and @tomato{1} into thin slices.
Cut @antipasti{8%oz}(ex. artichoke hearts, grilled peppers, or jarred mix) into bite-sized pieces and heat briefly in a pan.

Next, spread the @pesto{1%tbsp} onto the bread and place alternating layers of tomato and mozzarella slices on top.

Place the antipasti, @prosciutto di Parma{4%oz}, and the @arugula{1/4%cup} on the ciabatta.
Place another piece of bread on top.
Pierce with a wooden skewer to to make the sandwich easier to serve and eat.
